5. Section 28-A A of Land Acquisition Act, 1894 reads as under:
"28A. Re-determination determination of the amount of compensation on the basis of the award of the ourt.- (1) Where in an award under this P Court Part, the Court ourt allows to the applicant any amount of compensation in excess of the amount awarded byy the Collector under section 11,11, the persons interested in all the other land covered by the same notification under section 4, sub-section section (1) and who are also aggrieved by the award of the Collector may, notwithstanding that they had not made an application to the Collector under section 18, by written application to the Collector within three months from the date of the award of the Court C require that the amount of compensation payable to them may be re re- determined on the basis of the amount of compensation awarded by the Court;
